+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS=1, counts where the command reader waits for chip-written command list copies, what reads those words, the reader and recorder clocks, chip waits by thread, list macros' code and mesh draws in those lists (log only, off by default)
+
+Why: with frame ahead off the command reader (the GPU thread, the split's front) blocks about
+18.5 ms a frame in the area after the field and about 12 on the field in BufferCache::
+Nx2ReadListCopy -> WaitSubmittedTick, about 3.5 times a frame ('#1094' copy waits, run1548/1549).
+Nobody knows which list carries the long wait (macro 0xe74's grid words, 0xe62's mesh counts or
+another), what the macros do with the words, or how the reader's time splits. This is build A /
+stage 0b of our plan of 14 Nov for the command reader and the recording thread: counters
+only.
+
+What, with EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS=1 (exact "1", read once; new header
+src/video_core/listwait_stats.h holds the flag, the fixed-size counters and the small helpers):
+- buffer_cache.h Nx2ReadListCopy, blocking path only: the wait's length, and at its start the
+  chip's backlog (submitted ticks not finished, after one fence refresh:
+  BufferCacheRuntime::Nx2RefreshedGpuTick, new in vk_buffer_cache.h/.cpp, no Wait/Finish line) and
+  how many of those come before and with the copy's tick; handed to DmaPusher::Step through a
+  reader-only thread_local (ListWait::t_entry_wait).
+- dma_pusher.cpp Step: per entry read through the list copy path, what reads its words (the
+  method it continues, macros by their even method, with the engine and whether the entry is all
+  that method's data, its data then commands, or commands; else the first header's method), its
+  number since the last present, its size; waits binned (<0.1, 0.1-1, 1-5, 5-20, >=20 ms), per
+  kind (0xe74 / 0xe62 / other) and per consumer (16-slot table); the window's longest wait with
+  all of that. Once per engine and macro entry that reads chip-written words: 85 instructions /
+  255 words of its code from its start (or to the RAM's end; not cut at the first end bit, which
+  a branch can cancel: the line names that instruction), from the RAM it runs from (3D: the 3D
+  engine's; compute: KeplerCompute::ListWaitMacroRam, new in engines/kepler_compute.h/.cpp, the
+  RAM the compute engine picks now, null-safe), only where the reader owns that RAM (macros on the
+  front or no split); 0xe62 and 0xe74 always, at most 8 other macros a session, then one line.
+  Around ProcessCommands of such an entry, a deferred marker (FastDrawNeutral) on the recorder so
+  mesh draws inside it are counted.
+- DmaPusher::DispatchCalls, GpuSplit::WaitFor and DrainAt: the reader's clock (working, stopped
+  for the recorder inside list parsing or for other commands, blocked on the chip, idle), on the
+  marked GPU thread only.
+- GpuSplit::BackLoop: each out-of-work gap of the recorder (from running dry to its next entry,
+  across early wake-ups, its idle hook's time left out) in bins <0.1, 0.1-1, 1-5, >=5 ms, by what
+  the reader was doing when the gap began.
+- submit_stats.h WaitTimer (every MasterSemaphore::Wait past its quick checks): also counted by
+  the waiting thread (reader: GpuSplit::MarkGpuThread; recorder: BackLoop; fencing thread:
+  fence_manager.h ReleaseThreadFunc; other), by the waited tick's origin when
+  EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS=1 (else "other"). NoteFrame (only with EDEN_UP_SUBMIT_STATS=1) also counts
+  presents and their time for the list positions.
+- vk_rasterizer.cpp, after mesh_draw is known: mesh draws, and those inside a list-copy entry,
+  task or lone (unique_hashes[3] == 0, as the mesh census).
+- GpuSplit::ReportListWait (from MaybeStart, the GPU thread): the lines below every 10 s.
+Lines (HW_GPU info): boot "EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS=1 (log only: ...)"; every 10 s
+"EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS in T s, P presents: N list entries through the copy path, W waited; waits
+by length: ...; by what reads the words: ...; longest wait: ...; consumers: ...",
+"EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS reader in T s: working ... ms ...", "EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS recorder out of
+work in T s: ...", "EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS chip waits by waiting thread in T s ...: ...",
+"EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS mesh draws in T s: ..."; once per macro "EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS macro
+<3D|compute> macro 0x... (entry 0x.., start 0x..) reads chip-written list words: ..." then "...
+<3D|compute> macro 0x... words A-B: <hex words>".
+
+Unset: every new site tests a cached flag (function-local statics, read after env.txt) and does
+nothing else; no allocation, no wait, no message, no ring entry: as T185. Counting cost with it on:
+a clock pair per DispatchCalls, per reader wait for the recorder, per recorder gap and per chip
+wait, one fence refresh per blocking list copy wait, two deferred markers per list-copy entry, and
+the 10 s lines. None of the touched files is a translation id input (not under
+src/shader_recompiler, not in tools/gen-translation-id.py's SINGLE list, not reached from the
+translator's includes), no compile definition or include dir is added, no scheduler.Wait/Finish
+line is added to a cost file, and EDEN_UP_LISTWAIT_STATS is not in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE
+STORE.
